---@field lastVerificationTime? string Output only. Timestamp of the last successful verification for the endpoint, if any.

---@alias gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1EndpointVerificationInfoList gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1EndpointVerificationInfo[]

---The event being assessed.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1Event
---@field express? boolean Optional. Flag for a reCAPTCHA express request for an assessment without a token. If enabled, `site_key` must reference an Express site key.
---@field headers? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.StringList Optional. HTTP header information about the request.
---@field userInfo? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1UserInfo Optional. Information about the user that generates this event, when they can be identified. They are often identified through the use of an account for logged-in requests or login/registration requests, or by providing user identifiers for guest actions like checkout.
---@field ja3? string Optional. JA3 fingerprint for SSL clients. To learn how to compute this fingerprint, please refer to https://github.com/salesforce/ja3.
---@field userIpAddress? string Optional. The IP address in the request from the user's device related to this event.
---@field expectedAction? string Optional. The expected action for this type of event. This should be the same action provided at token generation time on client-side platforms already integrated with recaptcha enterprise. Required for Universal keys.
---@field transactionData? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1TransactionData Optional. Data describing a payment transaction to be assessed. Sending this data enables reCAPTCHA Enterprise Fraud Prevention and the FraudPreventionAssessment component in the response.
---@field userAgent? string Optional. The user agent present in the request from the user's device related to this event.
---@field ja4? string Optional. JA4 fingerprint for SSL clients. To learn how to compute this fingerprint, please refer to https://github.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4.
---@field wafTokenAssessment? boolean Optional. Flag for running Web Application Firewall (WAF) token assessment. If enabled, the token must be specified, and have been created by a WAF-enabled key.
---@field fraudPrevention? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1EventFraudPreventionEnum|string Optional. The Fraud Prevention setting for this assessment.
---@field hashedAccountId? string Optional. Deprecated: use `user_info.account_id` instead. Unique stable hashed user identifier for the request. The identifier must be hashed using hmac-sha256 with stable secret.
---@field firewallPolicyEvaluation? boolean Optional. Flag for enabling firewall policy config assessment. If this flag is enabled, the firewall policy is evaluated and a suggested firewall action is returned in the response.
---@field token? string Optional. The user response token provided by the reCAPTCHA Enterprise client-side integration on your site.
---@field requestedUri? string Optional. The URI resource the user requested that triggered an assessment.
---@field siteKey? string Optional. The site key that was used to invoke reCAPTCHA Enterprise on your site and generate the token.

---@alias gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1EventFraudPreventionEnum "FRAUD_PREVENTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"ENABLED"|"DISABLED"

---Settings specific to keys that can be used for reCAPTCHA Express.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1ExpressKeySettings

---An individual action. Each action represents what to do if a policy matches.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallAction
---@field block? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionBlockAction This action denies access to a given page. The user gets an HTTP error code.
---@field setHeader? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionSetHeaderAction This action sets a custom header but allow the request to continue to the customer backend.
---@field includeRecaptchaScript? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionIncludeRecaptchaScriptAction This action injects reCAPTCHA JavaScript code into the HTML page returned by the site backend.
---@field allow? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionAllowAction The user request did not match any policy and should be allowed access to the requested resource.
---@field substitute? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionSubstituteAction This action transparently serves a different page to an offending user.
---@field redirect? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionRedirectAction This action redirects the request to a reCAPTCHA interstitial to attach a token.

---An allow action continues processing a request unimpeded.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionAllowAction

---A block action serves an HTTP error code a prevents the request from hitting the backend.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionBlockAction

---An include reCAPTCHA script action involves injecting reCAPTCHA JavaScript code into the HTML returned by the site backend. This reCAPTCHA script is tasked with collecting user signals on the requested web page, issuing tokens as a cookie within the site domain, and enabling their utilization in subsequent page requests.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionIncludeRecaptchaScriptAction

---@alias gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionList gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallAction[]

---A redirect action returns a 307 (temporary redirect) response, pointing the user to a reCAPTCHA interstitial page to attach a token.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionRedirectAction

---A set header action sets a header and forwards the request to the backend. This can be used to trigger custom protection implemented on the backend.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionSetHeaderAction
---@field value? string Optional. The header value to set in the request to the backend server.
---@field key? string Optional. The header key to set in the request to the backend server.

---A substitute action transparently serves a different page than the one requested.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionSubstituteAction
---@field path? string Optional. The address to redirect to. The target is a relative path in the current host. Example: "/blog/404.html".

---A FirewallPolicy represents a single matching pattern and resulting actions to take.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallPolicy
---@field actions? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallActionList Optional. The actions that the caller should take regarding user access. There should be at most one terminal action. A terminal action is any action that forces a response, such as `AllowAction`, `BlockAction` or `SubstituteAction`. Zero or more non-terminal actions such as `SetHeader` might be specified. A single policy can contain up to 16 actions.
---@field path? string Optional. The path for which this policy applies, specified as a glob pattern. For more information on glob, see the [manual page](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/glob.7.html). A path has a max length of 200 characters.
---@field description? string Optional. A description of what this policy aims to achieve, for convenience purposes. The description can at most include 256 UTF-8 characters.
---@field condition? string Optional. A CEL (Common Expression Language) conditional expression that specifies if this policy applies to an incoming user request. If this condition evaluates to true and the requested path matched the path pattern, the associated actions should be executed by the caller. The condition string is checked for CEL syntax correctness on creation. For more information, see the [CEL spec](https://github.com/google/cel-spec) and its [language definition](https://github.com/google/cel-spec/blob/master/doc/langdef.md). A condition has a max length of 500 characters.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name for the FirewallPolicy in the format `projects/{project}/firewallpolicies/{firewallpolicy}`.

---Policy config assessment.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallPolicyAssessment
---@field firewallPolicy? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallPolicy Output only. The policy that matched the request. If more than one policy may match, this is the first match. If no policy matches the incoming request, the policy field is left empty.
---@field error? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleRpcStatus Output only. If the processing of a policy config fails, an error is populated and the firewall_policy is left empty.

---@alias gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallPolicyList gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FirewallPolicy[]

---Assessment for Fraud Prevention.
---@class gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FraudPreventionAssessment
---@field stolenInstrumentVerdict? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FraudPreventionAssessmentStolenInstrumentVerdict Output only. Assessment of this transaction for risk of a stolen instrument.
---@field behavioralTrustVerdict? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FraudPreventionAssessmentBehavioralTrustVerdict Output only. Assessment of this transaction for behavioral trust.
---@field cardTestingVerdict? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FraudPreventionAssessmentCardTestingVerdict Output only. Assessment of this transaction for risk of being part of a card testing attack.
---@field riskReasons? gcp.recaptchaenterprise_v1.GoogleCloudRecaptchaenterpriseV1FraudPreventionAssessmentRiskReasonList Output only. Reasons why the transaction is probably fraudulent and received a high transaction risk score.
---@field transactionRisk? number Output only. Probability of this transaction being fraudulent. Summarizes the combined risk of attack vectors below. Values are from 0.0 (lowest) to 1.0 (highest).

---Information about behavioral trust of the transaction.
